/	HELP LOADER GENERATOR FOR P?S/8

/	LAST EDIT: 27-SEP-2016 14:00 CJL
	XLIST	OFF			/TURN OFF LISTING.
	IFNDEF	OFF	<OFF=	1>	/TURN OFF LISTING DEFINITION.
	IFNDEF	ON	<ON=	0>	/TURN ON LISTING DEFINITION.
	XLIST	ON			/TURN LISTING ON.

/	MAY BE ASSEMBLED WITH THE '/J' OPTION SWITCH [PAL8 '/F' SWITCH] SET.

/	THIS IS THE ORIGINAL DEC-08-LHAA "HELP" LOADER AND GENERATOR UTILITY
/	01-APR-1967 FOR USE WITH THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER AND THE STANDARD
/	DEC RIM LOADER.

/	AS ORIGINALLY RELEASED, THE HELP LOADER WAS CREATED FROM A GENERATING PROGRAM
/	THAT APPENDED THE ORIGINAL DEC VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER DEC-08-LBAA
/	10-MAY-1967 [ACTUALLY A SOMEWHAT EARLIER VERSION THAT WAS SLIGHTLY DIFFERENT
/	BUT USES THE IDENTICAL INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS AND MEMORY LAYOUT] AND THE
/	STANDARD DEC RIM LOADER DEC-08-LRAA 23-FEB-1965 [OR THE HIGH-SPEED READER
/	VERSION RELEASED SOME TIME LATER].  THESE TWO UTILITIES ARE PRESUMED TO
/	ALREADY BE IN MEMORY [AND USED TO LOAD IN THE HELP LOADER GENERATING PROGRAM].

/	THIS RELEASE INCLUDES THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER AND THE STANDARD DEC
/	RIM LOADER USING A GLOBAL PARAMETER TO CHOSE THE LOW-SPEED OR HIGH-SPEED
/	VERSIONS OF BOTH LOADERS.  [NOTE: ALL VERSIONS OF THE RIM LOADER MUST BE
/	ASSEMBLED FOR THE INTENDED HARDWARE; ALL DEC VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER USE
/	THE FRONT PANEL SWITCHES TO MAKE A DYNAMIC CHOICE OF LOADING DEVICE.  THE
/	P?S/8 VERSION OF BIN IS ASSEMBLED IN A MANNER ANALOGOUS TO THE RIM LOADER.
/	SINCE THE P?S/8 VERSION OF BOTH LOADERS ARE ALWAYS LOADED FROM THE P?S/8
/	OPERATING SYSTEM, THERE IS NO REASON TO SUPPORT DYNAMIC LOADING DEVICE CHOICE
/	FOR THE BIN LOADER; WHEN THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY PROGRAM IS USED TO LOAD THESE
/	PAPER-TAPE LOADERS OVER THE OPERATING SYSTEM KERNEL, THE PROGRAM IS USED WITH
/	APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES TO DETERMINE THE HARDWARE DEVICE AND
/	CHOICE OF BIN OR RIM LOADER STARTUP.  THIS HAS THE ADDITIONAL ADVANTAGE OF
/	PROPER FUNCTIONING ON MACHINES LACKING FRONT PANELS SUCH AS THE OEM VERSION
/	OF THE PDP-8/M.

/	AS SUCH, THIS PROGRAM CAN GENERATE EITHER A LOW-SPEED VERSION OF THE ENTIRE
/	HELP LOADER OR A HIGH-SPEED VERSION OF THE ENTIRE PACKAGE BY CHANGING THE
/	GLOBAL READER DEVICE PARAMETER BELOW:

	IFNDEF	ASR	<ASR=	1>	/GENERATE THE LOW-SPEED READER
					/HELP LOADER BY DEFAULT.

	IFNDEF	APUNCH	<APUNCH=1>	/CREATE THE HELP LOADER PAPER-TAPE ON THE
					/LOW-SPEED PUNCH BY DEFAULT.

/	NOTE: THE ORIGINAL DEC RELEASE DOES NOT SUPPORT THE HIGH-SPEED READER OR THE
/	HIGH-SPEED PUNCH.

	NOPUNCH				/THE HELP LOADER IS NOT LOADED INTO MEMORY.
					/THE USER MUST DEPOSIT IT MANUALLY TO LOAD THE
					/HELP LOADER BINARY PAPER-TAPE CREATED BY THIS
					/PROGRAM.  BINARY OUTPUT WILL RESUME LATER TO
					/CREATE THE HELP LOADER GENERATOR PROGRAM AND
					/RELATED DATA.
/	HELP LOADER PROGRAM TO LOAD THE HIGH-SPEED HELP LOADER BINARY PAPER-TAPE.

	*26				/HIGH-SPEED HELP LOADER LOADS HERE.

	HSTART=	.			/LOAD AND START THE HIGH-SPEED HELP LOADER HERE.

/	THE HIGH-SPEED READER VERSION IS ONE WORD LONGER THAN THE LOW-SPEED VERSION.

	RFC				/START THE HIGH-SPEED PAPER-TAPE READER.

GO,	RSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	RFC RRB				/YES, GET THIS FRAME AND START THE NEXT ONE.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT LEADER FRAME.
	JMP	GO			/IGNORE AND WAIT FOR ANOTHER ONE.
	RTR;	RAR			/MOVE OVER THREE BITS.  [NOTE: LINK USED.]
INST,	DCA	LOADPTR			/STORE LATEST VALUE.  [NOTE: WILL BE MODIFIED.]
	ISZ	INST			/INCREMENT LOADING INSTRUCTION.
	JMP	GO			/KEEP GOING.

/	HELP LOADER PROGRAM TO LOAD THE LOW-SPEED HELP LOADER BINARY PAPER-TAPE.

	*27				/LOW-SPEED HELP LOADER LOADS HERE.

	LSTART=	.			/LOAD AND START THE LOW-SPEED HELP LOADER HERE.

GO,	KSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	KRB				/YES, GET THIS FRAME AND START THE NEXT ONE.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT LEADER FRAME.
	JMP	GO			/IGNORE AND WAIT FOR ANOTHER ONE.
	RTR;	RAR			/MOVE OVER THREE BITS.  [NOTE: LINK USED.]
INST,	DCA	LOADPTR			/STORE LATEST VALUE.  [NOTE: WILL BE MODIFIED.]
	ISZ	INST			/INCREMENT LOADING INSTRUCTION.
	JMP	GO			/KEEP GOING.
/	AS THE HELP LOADER PROCESSES THE HELP LOADER PAPER-TAPE, THE FOLLOWING MEMORY
/	LOCATIONS ARE LOADED [FROM HELP FORMAT BINARY DATA].

	*5				/AFFECTED MEMORY LOCATIONS START HERE.

HTEMP,	.-.				/HIGH-ORDER HALF-WORD TEMPORARY.  THIS LOCATION
					/IS NOT ACTUALLY LOADED BY THE HELP LOADER; IT
					/IS USED AS TEMPORARY STORAGE WHILE 12-BIT
					/DATA WORDS ARE BEING FORMED AND LOADED BY THE
					/SECONDARY LOADER.

HEND,	.-.				/USED AS THE OFFICIAL HLT AT THE END OF THE
					/LOADING OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS.  THIS
					/LOCATION IS NOT ACTUALLY LOADED BY THE HELP
					/LOADER; A "HLT" INSTRUCTION [7402] WILL BE
					/LOADED HERE BY THE SECONDARY LOADER.  WHEN THE
					/MACHINE STOPS HERE, THE USER CAN CHOOSE TO
					/RUN THE BIN OR RIM LOADER AT THE STANDARD
					/ADDRESSES [07777 OR 07756 RESPECTIVELY].

LOADPTR,HEND-1				/LOADING POINTER [WILL BE PRE-INCREMENTED
					/BEFORE USE].  WHEN THE SECONDARY LOADER IS IN
					/CONTROL, THE LOADING POINTER WILL BE UPDATED
					/TO 7577 TO ALLOW FURTHER LOADING OF
					/07600-07777 FROM THE HELP LOADER PAPER-TAPE.

	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<	XLIST	ON
GO2,	KSF				/NEXT FRAME AVAILABLE?
	JMP	GO2			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	KRB				/YES, READ IT IN AND START ANOTHER ONE.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	ASR	<	XLIST	ON
GO2,	RSF				/NEXT FRAME AVAILABLE?
	JMP	GO2			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	RFC RRB				/YES, READ IT IN AND START ANOTHER ONE.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	RTL;	RTL;	RTL		/MOVE UP HIGH-ORDER HALF
	DCA	HTEMP			/STASH IT FOR NOW.
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<	XLIST	ON
GO3,	KSF				/NEXT FRAME AVAILABLE?
	JMP	GO3			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	KRB				/YES, READ IT IN AND START ANOTHER ONE.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	ASR	<	XLIST	ON
GO3,	RSF				/NEXT FRAME AVAILABLE?
	JMP	GO3			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	RFC RRB				/YES, READ IT IN AND START ANOTHER ONE.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	TAD	HTEMP			/ADD ON HIGH-ORDER HALF.
STPTCH,	DCA	STPTCH			/WILL BE OVERLAID WITH "DCA I LOADPTR" [3407]
					/WHEN THE SECONDARY LOADER IS RUNNING.
	ISZ	LOADPTR			/BUMP TO NEXT ADDRESS.
	JMP	GO2			/KEEP GOING.

/	COMES HERE WHEN THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS HAVE BEEN COMPLETELY LOADED.  [NOTE:
/	IF THE HELP LOADER PAPER-TAPE GENERATOR IS LOADED BY THE P?S/8 SLURP LOADER
/	[WHICH IS RECOMMENDED], AN ADDED BENEFIT IS THE ADDITIONAL LOADING OF THE
/	RESTART CODE FOR P?S/8 AT 07600-07641 BY USING THE HELP LOADER AS REQUIRED.
/	IF THIS IS NOT DONE , ONLY THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS WILL BE LOADED
/	BY THE HELP LOADER.]

	JMP	HEND			/JUMP TO THE OFFICIAL HALT ADDRESS.

/	THE NEXT WORD OVERLAYS THE HELP LOADER TO START THE SECONDARY LOADER.

GO,	JMP	GO2			/GO START THE SECONDARY LOADER.
/	HELP LOADER DATA FORMAT CONSIDERATIONS.

/	ALL HELP DATA WORDS MUST HAVE BITS[3-6] SET TO ZERO [BECAUSE THESE BITS ARE
/	NOT STORED IN THE DATA FRAMES].  THIS IS ACHIEVED AS FOLLOWS:

/	1)  ALL MRI INSTRUCTIONS MUST ADDRESS OPERANDS ON PAGE ZERO AT AN ADDRESS OF
/	    LESS THAN 0040.

/	2)  ALL MRI INSTRUCTIONS MUST NOT BE INDIRECT.  [NOTE: ONE WORD OF THE
/	    SECONDARY LOADER CANNOT CONFORM TO THIS RESTRICTION.  AS SUCH, IT IS NOT
/	    INCLUDED IN THE HELP LOADER DATA STREAM; THE WORD IS LOADED BY THE
/	    SECONDARY LOADER AS A SELF-DIRECTED PATCH OVER ANOTHER CONFORMING
/	    INSTRUCTION THAT CARRIES OUT THE SELF-PATCH.]

/	3)  NO GROUP 2 OR GROUP 3 OPERATE INSTRUCTIONS ARE ALLOWED.

/	4)  GROUP 1 OPERATE INSTRUCTIONS MUST NOT INCLUDE CLA, CLL OR CMA OPERATIONS.

/	5)  IOT INSTRUCTIONS MUST USE DEVICE CODES LESS THAN 40.

/	HELP LOADER DATA WORD VALUES [12-BIT].  THESE VALUES MUST BE CONSISTENT WITH
/	THE CONTENTS OF LOCATIONS 00007-00027 AS DEFINED ABOVE.

	WORD01=	HEND-1			/00007 	LOADPTR,HEND-1

	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD02=	KSF			/00010	GO2,	KSF
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD02=	RSF			/00010  GO2,	RSF
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	WORD03=	JMP	GO2		/00011		JMP	GO2
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD04=	KRB			/00012		KRB
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD04=	RFC RRB			/00012		RFC RRB
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	WORD05=	RTL			/00013		RTL
	WORD06=	RTL			/00014		RTL
	WORD07=	RTL			/00015		RTL
	WORD10=	DCA	HTEMP		/00016		DCA	HTEMP
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD11=	KSF			/00017	GO3,	KSF
	XLIST	OFF	>	

	IFZERO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD11=	KSF			/00017	GO3,	RSF
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	WORD12=	JMP	GO3		/00020		JMP	GO3
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD13=	KRB			/00021		KRB
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	ASR	<
	XLIST	ON
	WORD13=	RFC RRB			/00021		RFC RRB
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	WORD14=	TAD	HTEMP		/00022		TAD	HTEMP
	WORD15=	DCA	STPTCH		/00023	STPTCH,	DCA	STPTCH
	WORD16=	ISZ	LOADPTR		/00024		ISZ	LOADPTR
	WORD17=	JMP	GO2		/00025		JMP	GO2
	WORD20=	JMP	HEND		/00026		JMP	HEND
	WORD21=	JMP	GO2		/00027		JMP	GO2

	WORD22=	0			/DUMMY WORD FOR CALCULATION PURPOSES ONLY.
/	PARTIAL DATA VALUE CALCULATIONS FOR HELP LOADER DATA WORDS.

/	BITS[0-1] ARE MOVED TO BITS[10-11] OF THE SAME DATA WORD.

/	BIT[2] IS MOVED TO BIT[9]; HOWEVER, THE RESULT IS USED IN THE CALCULATION OF
/	THE PREVIOUS DATA WORD.  AS SUCH, THE LATEST DATA WORD WILL INCLUDE BIT[2] OF
/	THE NEXT WORD [MOVED TO BIT[9]].

/	BITS[3-6] ARE REQUIRED TO BE ALL ZEROES [AND WILL BE VALIDATED AS SUCH]; THESE
/	BITS ARE NOT USED IN THE DATA CALCULATIONS.

/	BITS[7-11] WILL BE MOVED TO BITS[4-8] OF THE SAME DATA WORD.

/	FOR EACH HELP FORMAT DATA WORD, PARTIAL CALCULATIONS ARE USED FOR ALL BITS
/	USED IN THE DATA WORD.  [THE BIT DATA FOR BIT[2] IS CREATED SEPARATELY AS
/	THE THREE TERMS ARE COMBINED TO CREATE THE NEEDED HELP LOADER DATA FRAME.]

	W01H=	WORD01&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD01.
	W01L=	WORD01&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD01.

	IFNZRO	WORD01&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W02H=	WORD02&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD02.
	W02L=	WORD02&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD02.

	IFNZRO	WORD02&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W03H=	WORD03&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD03.
	W03L=	WORD03&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD03.

	IFNZRO	WORD03&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W04H=	WORD04&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD04.
	W04L=	WORD04&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD04.

	IFNZRO	WORD04&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W05H=	WORD05&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD05.
	W05L=	WORD05&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD05.

	IFNZRO	WORD05&0740	<ERROR	.>
	W06H=	WORD06&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD06.
	W06L=	WORD06&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD06.

	IFNZRO	WORD06&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W07H=	WORD07&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD07.
	W07L=	WORD07&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD07.

	IFNZRO	WORD07&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W10H=	WORD10&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD10.
	W10L=	WORD10&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD10.

	IFNZRO	WORD10&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W11H=	WORD11&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD11.
	W11L=	WORD11&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD11.

	IFNZRO	WORD11&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W12H=	WORD12&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD12.
	W12L=	WORD12&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD12.

	IFNZRO	WORD12&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W13H=	WORD13&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD13.
	W13L=	WORD13&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD13.

	IFNZRO	WORD13&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W14H=	WORD14&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD14.
	W14L=	WORD14&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD14.

	IFNZRO	WORD14&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W15H=	WORD15&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD15.
	W15L=	WORD15&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD15.

	IFNZRO	WORD15&0740	<ERROR	.>
	W16H=	WORD16&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD16.
	W16L=	WORD16&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD16.

	IFNZRO	WORD16&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W17H=	WORD17&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM WORD17.
	W17L=	WORD17&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM WORD17.

	IFNZRO	WORD17&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W20H=	WORD20&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM LATEST WORD.
	W20L=	WORD20&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM LATEST WORD.

	IFNZRO	WORD20&0740	<ERROR	.>


	W21H=	WORD21&6000%2000	/FIRST BIT GROUP FROM LATEST WORD.
	W21L=	WORD21&37^10		/SECOND BIT GROUP FROM LATEST WORD.

	IFNZRO	WORD21&0740	<ERROR	.>


	ENPUNCH				/RESTORE BINARY OUTPUT NOW.
/	THE PROGRAM STARTS HERE IF THE P?S/8 BIN AND RIM LOADERS SHOULD BE MOVED TO
/	07642-07777.

	*200				/THE USUAL STARTING PLACE.

	HBEGIN=	.			/START HERE TO USE THE P?S/8 BIN AND RIM
					/LOADERS INSTEAD OF WHAT IS CURRENTLY LOADED IN
					/07642-07777.

	ZBLOCK	376			/RESERVED FOR THE P?S/8 BIN AND RIM LOADERS
					/AND SUPPORT PROGRAMMING.

	JMP I	.+1;	PSTART		/NOW START THE HELP GENERATOR PROGRAM.
/	THE HELP GENERATOR PROGRAM STARTS HERE; ENSURE THAT THE CONTENTS OF LOCATIONS
/	07600-07777 ARE LOADED AS INTENDED AS THESE LOCATIONS WILL BE INCLUDED WITH
/	THE HELP LOADER BINARY DATA ON THE HELP BINARY PAPER-TAPE.

	*7400				/WHERE THE HELP GENERATOR LOADS.

PSTART,	CLA CLL				/CLEAN UP.
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	APUNCH	<
	XLIST	ON
	TLS				/INITIALIZE THE LOW-SPEED PUNCH.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	APUNCH	<
	XLIST	ON
	PLS				/INITIALIZE THE HIGH-SPEED PUNCH.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	TAD	KOUNT/(-27)		/SETUP THE AGGREGATE
	DCA	KOWNT			/HELP LOADER DATA COUNTER.
	TAD	BGIN/(HDATA)		/SETUP THE AGGREGATE
	DCA	START			/HELP LOADER DATA POINTER.

/	PUNCH BLANK LEADER FRAMES.

	TAD	BGIN/(-227)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	COUNT			/LEADER FRAME COUNTER.
	JMS	PUNCH			/PUNCH A BLANK LEADER FRAME.
	ISZ	COUNT			/DONE ENOUGH YET?
	JMP	.-2			/NO, KEEP GOING.
LOOP,	TAD I	START			/GET A HELP DATA FRAME WORD.
	JMS	PUNCH			/PUNCH IT.
	ISZ	START			/BUMP TO NEXT ONE.
	ISZ	KOWNT			/PUNCHED ALL OF THEM?
	JMP	LOOP			/NO, KEEP GOING.

/	THE CONTENTS OF 07600-07777 WILL BE PUNCHED IN SECONDARY LOADER FORMAT.

LOADER,	TAD I	START			/GET A LOADER [OR OTHER] WORD.
	RTR;RTR;RTR			/MOVE DOWN HIGH-ORDER HALF.
	AND	MASK/(77)		/JUST HIGH-ORDER BITS.
	JMS	PUNCH			/PUNCH HIGH-ORDER HALF NOW.
	TAD I	START			/GET THE WORD AGAIN.
	AND	MASK/(77)		/JUST LOW-ORDER BITS.
	JMS	PUNCH			/PUNCH LOW-ORDER HALF NOW.
	ISZ	START			/BUMP TO NEXT; ALSO DATA WORD COUNTER.
	JMP	LOADER			/KEEP GOING UNTIL ALL ARE PUNCHED.

/	PUNCH TRAILER FRAMES WITH HIGH-BIT SET.

	TAD	BGIN/(-227)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	COUNT			/TRAILER FRAME COUNTER.
	TAD	COD200/(200)		/GET TRAILER VALUE.
	JMS	PUNCH			/PUNCH A TRAILER FRAME.
	ISZ	COUNT			/PUNCHED ENOUGH?
	JMP	.-3			/NO, KEEP GOING.
	HLT				/YES, WE'RE DONE.
/	PAPER-TAPE PUNCH ROUTINE.

PUNCH,	.-.				/PUNCH OUTPUT ROUTINE.
	XLIST	OFF

	IFNZRO	APUNCH	<
	XLIST	ON
	TSF				/FLAG UP YET?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	TLS				/YES, OUTPUT THE FRAME NOW.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	IFZERO	APUNCH	<
	XLIST	ON
	PSF				/FLAG UP YET?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	PLS				/YES, OUTPUT THE FRAME NOW.
	XLIST	OFF	>

	XLIST	ON
	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	JMP I	PUNCH			/RETURN TO CALLER.

BGIN,	HDATA				/WHERE HELP FRAME DATA IS LOADED; ALSO USED AS
					/A COUNTER WHEN PUNCHING THE LOADERS, ETC.
COUNT,	.-.				/FRAME COUNTER.
MASK,	77				/SIX-BIT DATA MASK.
KOUNT,	-27				/COUNT OF HELP DATA FRAMES TO BE PUNCHED.
KOWNT,	.-.				/HELP DATA FRAME PUNCH COUNTER.
COD200,	200				/HI-BIT OF PAPER-TAPE FRAMES [CONSTANT].
START,	.-.				/ADDRESS POINTER FOR 07600-07777 DATA.

	NOPUNCH				/TURN OFF BINARY OUTPUT FOR NOW.

	ZBLOCK	7551-.			/EMPTY SPACE.

	ENPUNCH				/RESTORE BINARY OUTPUT.

	*.				/RESTABLISH OUR ORIGIN.

/	HELP LOADER DATA WORDS.

/	ALL DATA VALUES MUST BE LESS THAN 0377 [AND WILL BE PUNCHED AS EIGHT-BIT
/	PAPER-TAPE FRAMES].  THE DATA FORMAT IS AS DETAILED ABOVE.

	HDATA=	.			/HELP LOADER DATA WORDS START HERE.

/	COMBINED DATA WORD		 ADDRESS  VALUE  SOURCE TEXT

	WORD02&1000%200+W01H+W01L	/00007    0005   "HEND-1"
	WORD03&1000%200+W02H+W02L	/00010    6031   "KSF"     OR   6011 "RSF"
	WORD04&1000%200+W03H+W03L	/00011    5010   "JMP GO2"	
	WORD05&1000%200+W04H+W04L	/00012    6036   "KRB"     OR   6016 "RFC RRB"
	WORD06&1000%200+W05H+W05L	/00013    7006   "RTL"
	WORD07&1000%200+W06H+W06L	/00014    7006   "RTL"
	WORD10&1000%200+W07H+W07L	/00015    7006   "RTL"
	WORD11&1000%200+W10H+W10L	/00016    3005   "DCA HTEMP"
	WORD12&1000%200+W11H+W11L	/00017    6031   "KSF"     OR   6011 "RSF"
	WORD13&1000%200+W12H+W12L	/00020    5017	 "JMP GO3"
	WORD14&1000%200+W13H+W13L	/00021    6036   "KRB"     OR   6016 "RFC RRB"
	WORD15&1000%200+W14H+W14L	/00022    1005   "TAD HTEMP"
	WORD16&1000%200+W15H+W15L	/00023    3023   "DCA STPTCH"
	WORD17&1000%200+W16H+W16L	/00024    2007   "ISZ LOADPTR"
	WORD20&1000%200+W17H+W17L	/00025    5010   "JMP GO2"
	WORD21&1000%200+W20H+W20L	/00026    5006   "JMP HEND"
	WORD22&1000%200+W21H+W21L	/00027    5010   "JMP GO2"

/	SECONDARY LOADER DATA WORDS.

/	SECONDARY LOADER DATA WORDS CONTAIN 12-BIT DATA IN TWO ADJACENT WORDS.  THE
/	FIRST WORD CONTAINS BITS[0-5] MOVED TO BITS[6-11].  THE SECOND WORD CONTAINS
/	BITS[6-11].  [ALL VALUES ARE LESS THAN 0377.]  THREE DATA WORD PAIRS ARE
/	DEFINED AS FOLLOWS:

/	1)	LOCATION "STPTCH" [0023] OF THE SECONDARY LOADER CONTAINS
/		"DCA STPTCH" [3023]:

/		STPTCH,	DCA	STPTCH	/STORE THE FIRST DATA WORD OVER INSTRUCTION.

/		THE REPLACEMENT DATA IS "DCA I LOADPTR" [3407].  DUE TO THE
/		RESTRICTIONS OF THE HELP LOADER, THIS VALUE COULD NOT BE LOADED
/		DIRECTLY.  ONCE THIS INSTRUCTION IS REPLACED, ADDITIONAL WORDS WILL
/		BE STORED INDIRECTLY USING "LOADPTR" [0007].  LOCATION 0007 WAS
/		INITIALLY LOADED WITH "HEND-1" [0005]; HOWEVER, AFTER THE INSTRUCTION
/		IS MODIFIED, THE CONTENTS OF 0007 ARE INCREMENTED TO POINT TO "HEND"
/		[0006]  [BY ANOTHER WORD WITHIN THE SECONDARY LOADER].

	SWORD1=	DCA I	LOADPTR		/TO BE LOADED OVER "STPTCH" [0023].
/	2)	LOCATION "HEND" [0006] CONTAINS 0000 WHICH IS CHANGED TO A "HLT"
/		[7402] INSTRUCTION.  [NOTE: LOCATION "HEND" [0006] IS NOT EXECUTED
/		WHILE THE CONTENTS ARE 0000.]

/		DUE TO THE RESTRICTIONS OF THE HELP LOADER, THIS VALUE COULD NOT BE
/		LOADED DIRECTLY.  AFTER THE "HLT" [7402] INSTRUCTION IS STORED OVER
/		"HEND" [0006], "LOADPTR" [0007] IS INCREMENTED TO POINT TO "LOADPTR"
/		[0007].

/		WHEN THE SECONDARY LOADER [EVENTUALLY] FINISHES ALL OF THE LOADING
/		OPERATIONS, THE COMPUTER MUST BE STOPPED TO ALLOW THE USER TO CHOOSE
/		THE NEXT TASK [SUCH AS STARTING THE RIM OR BIN LOADER].  THE COMPUTER
/		HALTS AT "HEND" [0006] SIGNALING THE END OF THE ENTIRE HELP LOADING
/		PROCESS.  [NOTE: WHILE THE HELP LOADER IS INCAPABLE OF LOADING A "HLT"
/		[7402] INSTRUCTION, A "JMP HEND" [5206] INSTRUCTION IS EXECUTED [AFTER
/		THE "HLT" [7402] INSTRUCTION IS IN PLACE] TO END THE SECONDARY LOADING
/		OPERATION.]

	SWORD2=	HLT			/TO BE LOADED OVER "HEND" [0006].

/	3)	LOCATION "LOADPTR" [0007] CONTAINS "LOADPTR" [0007] WHICH IS CHANGED
/		TO 7577.

/		THE "LOADPTR" [0007] LOCATION POINTS TO ITSELF.  THE ADDRESS OF THE
/		LOWEST LOCATION OF THE LAST PAGE OF MEMORY [07600] IS LOADED INTO
/		"LOADPTR" [0007] TO ALLOW THE PREVIOUS CONTENTS OF 07600-07777 TO BE
/		RESTORED.  [NOTE: DUE TO THE PRE-INCREMENT OPERATION OF THE SECONDARY
/		LOADER, THE ACTUAL VALUE LOADED IS 7577.]

/		NOTE: THE PREVIOUS CONTENTS OF 07600-07777 MAY CONTAIN THE BIN AND RIM
/		LOADERS OR THE KERNEL OF AN OPERATING SYSTEM SUCH AS P?S/8; THE EXACT
/		CONTENTS IS DETERMINED WHEN THE HELP GENERATOR PROGRAM IS STARTED AT
/		"PSTART" [07400].  AN INCLUDED VARIANT IS ACHIEVED BY STARTING AT
/		"HBEGIN" [00200].  THIS WILL MOVE THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER
/		AND THE STANDARD RIM LOADER INTO 07642-07777.  DEPENDING ON THE
/		SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION OF P?S/8, A VERSION-SPECIFIC P?S/8 BOOTSTRAP
/		MAY BE INCLUDED IN 07600-07641 [IF SUPPORTED AND THE BINARY OUTPUT OF
/		THIS PROGRAM IS LOADED BY THE P?S/8 "SLURP" LOADER, IF APPLICABLE].
/		FOR CERTAIN SPECIFIC P?S/8 CONFIGURATIONS, THE CONTENTS OF 07600-07777
/		WILL CONTAIN THE COMPLETE P?S/8 SYSTEM KERNEL; STARTING AT "PSTART"
/		[07400] WILL CREATE THIS VARIANT HELP LOADER PACKAGE.  BY ORIGINAL
/		DESIGN, THE PROGRAM ASSUMES THE DEC STANDARD BIN AND RIM LOADERS ARE
/		LOADED.  WHEN RUNNING THIS HELP GENERATOR PROGRAM, CONFIGURE THE
/		CONTENTS OF 07600-07777 ACCORDINGLY.

	SWORD3=	7577			/TO BE LOADED OVER "LOADPTR" [0007].

	SWORD1%100			/HIGH-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 1.
	SWORD1&77			/LOW-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 1.
	SWORD2%100			/HIGH-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 2.
	SWORD2&77			/LOW-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 2.
	SWORD3%100			/HIGH-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 3.
	SWORD3&77			/LOW-ORDER HALF OF SECONDARY LOADER WORD 3.

	IFNZRO	7600-.	<ERROR	.>	/THE LAST WORD SHOULD LOAD INTO 07577.
