/	THIS PAGE WILL BE LOADED WITH THE INTENDED LOADERS TO BE INCLUDED WITH THE
/	HELP LOADER PACKAGE.  THE HELP PROCESS DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE BETWEEN LOADER
/	CODE AND UNUSED LOCATIONS.

/	AS SUCH, OPERATING SYSTEM KERNELS SUCH AS THE P?S/8 SYSTEM KERNEL [ASSUMING
/	NO EXTENDED MEMORY CONSIDERATIONS ARE PRESENT] CAN BE LOADED ONTO A CUSTOM
/	HELP LOADER PAPER-TAPE.  THE EXPECTED CONTENTS ARE THE BIN AND RIM LOADER.

/	NOTE: CERTAIN VERSIONS OF P?S/8 SUPPORT A STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP LOADED INTO
/	07600-07641 WHEN THE P?S/8 "SLURP" LOADER IS USED TO LOAD THE HELP GENERATOR
/	PROGRAM.  THIS PROGRAM INCLUDES A COPY OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS AS USED IN
/	P?S/8 VERSION 9A [CURRENTLY BEING DEVELOPED]; THE P?S/8 VERSION 8Z RELEASE FOR
/	TC01/TC08/TU55/TU56 IS COMPATIBLE WITH THESE LOADERS [AND CAN LOAD THE HELP
/	GENERATOR PROGRAM WITH THE "SLURP" LOADER BY USING THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY
/	WITH CERTAIN COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS SET ACCORDINGLY:

/	/F - THIS OPTION SWITCH MUST BE CLEAR TO PREVENT USE OF THE HIGH-SPEED READER
/	     OR HIGH-SPEED PUNCH.

/	/I - THIS OPTION SWITCH MUST BE CLEAR TO PREVENT THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER
/	     FROM BEING RELOADED OVER THE "SLURP" LOADER.

/	/P - THIS OPTION SWITCH MUST BE CLEAR TO PREVENT THE USE OF BINARY PAPER-TAPE
/	     DATA INSTEAD BINARY FILE LOADING.

/	/V - THIS OPTION SWITCH MUST BE CLEAR TO PREVENT USE OF THE VIRTUAL LOADER
/	     INSTEAD OF THE SLURP LOADER.

/	/W - THIS OPTION SWITCH MUST BE CLEAR TO PREVENT CREATION OF BINARY PAPER-TAPE
/	     OUTPUT INSTEAD OF BINARY FILE LOADING.

/	ALL OTHER OPTION SWITCHES THAT AFFECT BINARY LOADING MAY BE USED; FOR MORE
/	INFORMATION CONSULT ADVANCED DOCUMENTATION OF THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY PROGRAM.

